# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kartikeya Sharma et al. (2025). Accelerating point defect photo-emission calculations with machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-025-01820-1  arXiv:2505.01403v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.01403v2 (sha256 8158d430b6ac5166...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 145 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper uses seven
# pretrained universal MLIPs (MatterSim-v1-5M, MACE-MPA-0, M3GNet,
# SevenNet-0, MACE-MP-0, eqV2-M, ORB-v2) to compute defect phonons and
# compares the resulting Huang-Rhys factors with DFT (GPAW, PBE) for 791
# point defects in ten 2D hosts. It trains no model and reports no
# energy, force or stress error. Read from the arXiv preprint (v2).

