# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The only accuracy table (Table I) is on the dimensionless Huang-Rhys factor: MAE / RMSE / max error of 0.8 / 1.4 / 12.7 (MatterSim-v1-5M), 1.0 / 1.5 / 12.2 (MACE-MPA-0), 1.2 / 1.9 / 17.8 (M3GNet), 1.3 / 1.8 / 10.4 (SevenNet-0), 1.5 / 3.9 / 57.7 (MACE-MP-0), 1.9 / 2.5 / 10.8 (eqV2-M), 4.5 / 5.2 / 19.0 (ORB-v2). Schema 0.1.2 has no MetricProperty for it, so nothing is encoded; with a 'Huang-Rhys factor' (or generic derived-property) individual these seven rows would link to registry models.
# - Model releases are named only as above (no checkpoint for M3GNet, SevenNet-0 or MACE-MP-0), which would also have to be pinned before linking. The manifest classes the paper as 'Application/model instance'.
# - Read from the arXiv v2 preprint; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
